function riskScore(prompt) {
  let score = 0;
  if (/\b(email|e-mail|phone)\b/i.test(prompt)) score += 3;
  if (/\b(export|download|CSV|exported)\b/i.test(prompt)) score += 2;
  if (prompt.toLowerCase().includes("system prompt")) score += 4;
  return Math.min(score, 10);
}
function mitigate(prompt) {
  return prompt
    .replace(/[A-Za-z0-9._%+-]+@[A-Za-z0-9.-]+\.[A-Za-z]{2,}/g, "[REDACTED_EMAIL]")
    .replace(/\b\d{3}[-.\s]?\d{3}[-.\s]?\d{4}\b/g, "[REDACTED_PHONE]");
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you adapt this for multi-tenant workloads with different policy baselines?
- What tests would you add to validate redactions without affecting legitimate outputs?

## Why This Is Asked

This question tests ability to design cost-aware prompt orchestration, a practical constraint in cloud analytics workflows.

## Key Concepts

- Token cost estimation
- Budget-constrained orchestration
- Module selection strategy
- Latency-awareness

## Code Example

```javascript
function estimateTokens(prompt, overhead = 20) {
  return prompt.split(/\s+/).length + overhead;
}

function selectModules(prompt, budget, candidates) {
  let total = 0;
  const chosen = [];
  for (const [name, cost] of candidates) {
    if (total + cost <= budget) {
      chosen.push(name);
      total += cost;
    }
  }
  return chosen;
}
```

